	"summary": "One compiled standard library for every project (T-0182), the LTO fallback remembered (T-0183), imported headers kept on disk (T-0101), objects judged by size and time (T-0186), generic instance bodies defined once rather than in every header (T-0185), and g++ given an inline function's budget (T-0190). A build from clean now costs what a one-line change does: 0.31-0.45 s in debug, against 0.28-0.47 s for C++, and in release 1.25-1.9x the C++ build, from 2.2-2.9x. Importing stdlib.h falls from 85 ms to 2 ms. With g++ every program runs faster: A* search 0.83x C++, the word count 0.86x.",
